    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d549">

                <pb facs="0815" n="787" xml:id="pg787"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">310.2/9–1354: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Mission at the United
                        Nations</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d549-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">official use only</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-09-14T19:03:00-04:00">September 14,
                            1954—7:03 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>146. Urtel 229 re Chinese representation. Department accepts moratorium formula
                    proposed by Dixon but would prefer use phrase “during the current year” instead
                    of “during 1954”. Please so inform Dixon. If British unwilling accept this
                    change you are authorized inform Dixon we agree to formula as set forth
                    urtel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d549-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d549-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by the Deputy Director of the Office of UN Political and Security Affairs
                    (Bond), cleared by the Bureau of Far Eastern Affairs and the Bureau of European
                    Affairs, and signed by Assistant Secretary Key.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
